  "id": "c4xa4lg",
  "title": "Chapter 31: Interior of the Earth",
  "order": 32,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ztktkzu",
      "content": "The interior of the Earth consists of several layers that differ in composition, density, temperature and physical state. Knowledge about Earth's interior helps explain earthquakes, volcanic activity, plate tectonics and the formation of mountains."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
