    {
      "id": "f03xsk3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Sources of Information about Earth's Interior"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Direct sources of interior information include deep mining and volcanic eruptions, while indirect sources include seismic waves, meteors, and gravity.",
        "Primary (P) waves travel through solids, liquids, and gases, whereas Secondary (S) waves travel only through solids.",
        "The Earth's crust is divided into continental crust (SIAL: Silica and Aluminium) and oceanic crust (SIMA: Silica and Magnesium).",
        "The Mantle extends up to a depth of 2,900 km and accounts for nearly 84% of the Earth's volume.",
        "The Core is composed primarily of Heavy elements (Nickel and Iron) and is split into a liquid Outer Core and a solid Inner Core."
      ],
      "id": "f8bntaf"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2i1n2dc",
      "content": "Direct Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "izr4gix",
      "content": "• Deep mining operations."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c4zcark",
      "content": "• Scientific drilling projects."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2zxtbx3",
      "content": "• Volcanic eruptions which bring material from inside the Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1kudy3d",
      "content": "Indirect Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8jk774g",
      "content": "• Seismic waves generated by earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "geir8f8",
      "content": "• Study of meteorites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "two8q5m",
      "content": "• Gravitational and magnetic field studies."
    },
    {
      "id": "aq87cex",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Seismic Waves"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lppjnd9",
      "content": "• Seismic waves are energy waves generated during earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6zw5doy",
      "content": "• They help scientists understand the structure of Earth's interior."
    },
    {
      "id": "2pa251v",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Wave Type</strong></p>",
