    {
      "id": "zkg781x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Mantle"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ge9iv3a",
      "content": "• Lies below the crust and extends up to 2900 km depth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3pfpyna",
      "content": "• Forms about 84% of Earth's volume."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r1kgffl",
      "content": "• The upper part with the crust forms the lithosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0pd997h",
      "content": "• Below the lithosphere lies the asthenosphere where tectonic plates move."
    },
    {
      "id": "tywagtb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Core"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5frk5cu",
      "content": "• The core extends from 2900 km depth to the center of the Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6t6k552",
      "content": "• It is mainly composed of iron and nickel."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fh0swqx",
      "content": "• Temperatures may exceed 5000°C."
    },
    {
      "id": "awqxi8l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Core"
    },
